WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.988
(piano notes)

00:00:00.988 --> 00:00:03.371
(group chanting)

00:00:03.371 --> 00:00:05.400
(group screaming)

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.520
- I joined Team Indigenous to be a part

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.353
of something bigger than myself.

00:00:08.353 --> 00:00:11.040
- It's very important
that we have visibility

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.240
as native people.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.380
- I just think it's like
important to see somebody

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.869
that looks like you at the top level.

00:00:16.869 --> 00:00:18.900
(happy string music)

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.056
- [Narrator] This Great Big
Story is brought to you by Delta:

00:00:22.056 --> 00:00:23.990
When we venture out into the world,

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.260
we see all that we share.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:30.093
(group chanting and shouting)

00:00:32.342 --> 00:00:34.280
(fast string music)

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.310
- I'm April Fournier,
and I've been playing

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.650
roller derby for five years,

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.579
and I'm the co-founder of Team Indigenous.

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:41.412
(fast string music)

00:00:41.412 --> 00:00:43.790
Team Indigenous is a roller
derby team made up of

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.539
indigenous athletes from
all across the world.

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:48.621
- I think everything looks good,

00:00:48.621 --> 00:00:50.730
so we wanna really trust each
other and trust ourselves.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:53.580
- [April] The lack of representation
for indigenous nations

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:57.740
really fueled the reason that
we wanted to develop this team

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:02.310
and create this space for other
indigenous athletes to join

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.430
and compete against all
of these other nations

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.723
because we are a nation.

00:01:05.723 --> 00:01:06.556
- Nice.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.101
Let's do that again.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.481
(cars driving)

00:01:11.481 --> 00:01:13.150
(upbeat string music)

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:16.183
- I've played sports all my
life, and just nothing ever

00:01:16.183 --> 00:01:20.050
captured my attention
as much as roller derby.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:23.060
Living in Maine, no one else
really kind of understands

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.020
what it's like to kind of
be the only person of color

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.370
skating on a team.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:31.752
One day I saw a skater that
was on one of the best teams

00:01:31.752 --> 00:01:34.820
in the world and she looked like me.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.670
And ultimately from that we
came up with Team Indigenous.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.833
(bright piano music)

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.890
Hey everybody!

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.890
Hope all is well, so good to see you.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.351
Having teammates from
Canada, all around the U.S.,

00:01:54.351 --> 00:01:57.380
and South America, the way
that we're able to communicate

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.330
is through video conferencing.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.260
If you haven't seen any of
the updates, our first game is

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:05.660
against team Japan,
which is really exciting.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.350
Team Indigenous will be
at RollerCon participating

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.150
in the Nations Tournament.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.810
RollerCon is a roller derby
convention in Las Vegas,

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:18.240
that is seminars, on-skate
training, tournaments.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.160
It's just this really giant celebration of

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.510
the roller derby community.

00:02:23.504 --> 00:02:25.457
(upbeat piano music)

00:02:25.457 --> 00:02:27.056
(whistle blows)

00:02:27.056 --> 00:02:30.280
- When I play roller
derby, being in that pack,

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.260
being in that mix, there's
just no other feeling like it.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.470
There's so many different
friends and skaters

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:37.810
that look like me.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:41.683
They talk like me; they have
similar life experiences.

00:02:42.854 --> 00:02:46.670
(fast upbeat string music)

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.600
- Team Indigenous is absolutely
not about wins and loses;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.690
it's about being able to
take the track together

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.590
and see your siblings;

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:00.586
and you're all representing
together on the track as one.

00:03:00.586 --> 00:03:03.180
It's not something that you can quantify.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.440
It's not something that you can measure;

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.260
it's just community, it's
nation, it's indigenous,

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.851
and that's what we are.

00:03:09.851 --> 00:03:13.434
(fast upbeat string music)

00:03:16.144 --> 00:03:18.061
(bing)

